<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28011" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">marcor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		marceo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a withering</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">segetum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 3, 27, 4</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Decay, rottenness</i> (not anteAug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">panni marcor,</span>”
				<i>a rotten rag</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					22, 22, 46, § 94</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Faintness, languor, indolence</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">marcor, et inexpugnabilis dormiendi necessitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					3, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cernitis expositas turpi marcore cohortes, i.
					e. somno,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 10, 269</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maeror marcorque,</span>”
				<i>melancholy</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Tranq. 2, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ducis,</span>”
				<i>indolence, worthlessness</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vell. 2, 119, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
